# Performance

## Philosophy

Fast, smooth, responsive, lightweight. Performance beats visual complexity. Prioritize low-end Android and slow mobile networks.

## Rendering

- Prefer **React Server Components** and server actions
- Reduce client JS; use `next/dynamic` for below-the-fold: Gallery, RSVP, Maps
- Avoid unnecessary `"use client"` boundaries

## Bundles

Check impact before new dependencies; prefer lightweight alternatives.

## Images

- **`next/image`** with correct `sizes` (e.g. `(max-width: 768px) 100vw, 50vw`)
- WebP/AVIF; compress uploads; lazy load
- No large `background-image` for photos — use positioned `next/image`

## Motion

- Animate only **`transform`** and **`opacity`** (Framer Motion)
- No animating `height`, `box-shadow`, or layout properties
- **`backdrop-filter: blur()`** — desktop breakpoints only
- Ambient loops: CSS `@keyframes`, not infinite JS loops

## Scroll

Native browser scrolling only — no smooth-scroll / scroll-jacking libraries.

## Hydration

Time-sensitive UI (countdown): render generic/empty on server; compute delta in `useEffect` on client to avoid mismatch.

## State & Data

- Minimize rerenders; modular Zustand; selective subscriptions
- Fetch only required fields; avoid duplicate requests and polling

## Public Pages (`/w/[slug]`)

Critical path: fast first paint from WhatsApp. Avoid heavy video backgrounds, oversized hero media, animation showcases.

## Editor

Instant typing; debounced autosave (500–1500ms); no blocking saves or iframe reload loops.

## Fonts

Max 2 families; limited weights; `font-display: swap`.

## Lighthouse

Target strong mobile scores without sacrificing usability.

## Caching

Cache static assets and templates; don't cache stale critical user draft data incorrectly.
